# Dependencies & tooling — ask before adding

## Context

`app/package.json` has exactly two devDependencies (`typescript`, `vitest`)
and three scripts (`test`, `test:watch`, `typecheck`). A lint step is
intentionally NOT configured. Adding packages or config files silently changes
the exercise's architecture and the reviewer's environment.

## Rule

- NEVER run `npm install <pkg>` / add entries to `dependencies` or
  `devDependencies` without explicit approval in the conversation. Propose the
  package, the reason, and a zero-dependency alternative first.
- Prefer the standard library and the existing in-house helpers
  (`app/src/lib/text.ts`) over any package (uuid, lodash, date-fns, immer,
  slugify, …).
- NEVER add new tooling/config files (`.eslintrc*`, `eslint.config.*`,
  `.prettierrc*`, `vitest.config.*`, `jest.config.*`, bundler configs) or new
  npm scripts without approval.
- Do not invent commands that do not exist: the available ones are
  `cd app && npm test`, `npm run test:watch`, `npm run typecheck`. There is NO
  lint script — say so instead of running or documenting one.
- Do not change `app/tsconfig.json` (strict, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`) to
  make code compile — fix the code instead.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/package.json app/package-lock.json app/tsconfig.json` → empty
   unless the addition was explicitly approved.
2. `git status --porcelain app` → no new `*.config.*` / `.eslintrc*` /
   `.prettierrc*` files.
3. `grep -rn "from \"" app/src | grep -vE "\./|vitest"` → zero third-party
   imports.
4. `cd app && npm test && npm run typecheck` — green with the existing
   toolchain only.

